From 7fcd4b9f4f038ed0f5a0e2cfbf6af27a0a12bdd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:29:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(setup): setups keep their creation order, not their
 name order

A setup added second (datum_from the first) was listed and posted first
when its name sorted earlier. SetupDef now stores an order; CreateSetup
writes the next one, setup::setups sorts by it, and the project file
saves it as an additive key. Setups without the key (older files) keep
name order. The reorder command is filed as #3484.

Fixes #3447

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
